WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:03.197
Aleksei: Many people
ask me weird questions,

00:00:03.197 --> 00:00:07.300
and one of them is,
"Aleksei, do you have bones?"

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:09.710
and I often say, "Yes, I do have bones,

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:12.130
but before I go to work,
I leave them at home."

00:00:12.130 --> 00:00:14.170
Narrator: This is Aleksei Goloborodko,

00:00:14.170 --> 00:00:16.250
the world's best contortionist.

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:18.411
Aleksei: I train three
to five hours per day

00:00:18.411 --> 00:00:20.460
to maintain my flexibility and

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:24.570
my other disciplines
that I have in my act.

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:27.223
I control my body in all the shapes,

00:00:27.223 --> 00:00:29.273
all the positions that I want.

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:33.759
It feels awesome. It's
like having a superpower.

00:00:33.759 --> 00:00:35.150
Narrator: Aleksei is a
contortionist for the

00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:36.856
traveling circus company Cirque du Soleil.

00:00:36.856 --> 00:00:38.850
He's one of 45 performers

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:40.284
from 19 different nationalities

00:00:40.284 --> 00:00:42.729
traveling with the show "Luzia."

00:00:42.729 --> 00:00:44.680
Aleksei grew up in Tula, Russia,

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:46.510
and has been practicing contortionism

00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:48.480
since he was just 4 years old.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:50.900
Aleksei: When I was a kid, I
asked my parents to take me

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:53.060
to circus show, just
to watch them perform,

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:54.991
and the next day, I asked
my mom to take me to

00:00:54.991 --> 00:00:58.466
circus studio. I told her that
I fell in love with circus,

00:00:58.466 --> 00:01:00.680
and since then, I've
been doing contortion,

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:02.120
and it's almost 20 years.

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:04.958
I started when I was 4. Now I'm 24.

00:01:04.958 --> 00:01:06.070
Narrator: Aleksei began performing with

00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:08.280
Cirque du Soleil's
"Luzia" three years ago.

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:11.100
His show celebrates the
culture, history, and mythology

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:13.350
of Mexico by bringing to life a surreal

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:15.060
Mexican-themed dream.

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:17.190
It was the first Cirque du
Soleil show to incorporate

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:18.930
water into the set design.

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:21.120
Aleksei has been traveling
and contorting with "Luzia"

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:23.567
for hundreds of shows
across North America,

00:01:23.567 --> 00:01:26.248
and he quickly gained fame for
his mind-bending movements.

00:01:26.248 --> 00:01:28.569
Aleksei: It's a huge
responsibility to be the best

00:01:28.569 --> 00:01:31.648
contortionist in the world,
to be the most flexible male

00:01:31.648 --> 00:01:34.058
in the world, because I have many fans,

00:01:34.058 --> 00:01:37.978
and it's a huge responsibility
not to drop your level

00:01:37.978 --> 00:01:41.147
from here to there because
if you drop your level,

00:01:41.147 --> 00:01:42.600
you disappoint them, and I feel like

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:45.310
I don't have rights to
disappoint my public.

00:01:45.310 --> 00:01:48.107
I don't have rights to
disappoint my people.

00:01:48.107 --> 00:01:50.140
Narrator: We caught up with
Aleksei during his warm-up

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:52.105
before the premiere of
"Luzia" in New York City.

00:01:52.105 --> 00:01:54.070
Aleksei: My genre is
called dancing contortion.

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:56.454
It's a mix of different disciplines,

00:01:56.454 --> 00:01:59.940
and the base is contortion,
being bendy and flexible,

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:01.945
and other disciplines
such as hand balance,

00:02:01.945 --> 00:02:05.820
elements of rhythmic gymnastics,
elements of ballet dance,

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:09.744
elements of modern dance
are maintained in my act.

00:02:09.744 --> 00:02:11.591
Narrator: Aleksei warms up for about 40

00:02:11.591 --> 00:02:13.450
to 45 minutes before each show.

00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:15.580
It's one of five stretching
and cardio sessions

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:17.970
he has throughout the day.
He has to keep his body

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:20.316
limber and loose so he
doesn't hurt himself.

00:02:20.316 --> 00:02:22.890
Aleksei: For practice for
training, I'm very aware of

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:25.921
each movement I do because when I stretch,

00:02:25.921 --> 00:02:29.730
I have to keep everything under control

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:32.470
not to injure myself, but when I perform,

00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:35.888
I mostly think about my
character in the act.

00:02:35.888 --> 00:02:38.363
I think about my presence on stage.

00:02:38.363 --> 00:02:40.070
Narrator: Not only does Aleksei constantly

00:02:40.070 --> 00:02:42.700
have to strengthen his
body, but contortionism also

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:45.753
demands a steady mind.
It's similar to yoga,

00:02:45.753 --> 00:02:47.580
and he has to learn to
control his thoughts,

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:49.599
be present with his body
through each movement.

00:02:49.599 --> 00:02:51.991
Aleksei: The hardest part
is to maintain the balance

00:02:51.991 --> 00:02:54.533
between flexibility and strength

00:02:54.533 --> 00:02:58.100
because if I get too loose, too flexible,

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:00.010
and I don't care about my strength,

00:03:00.010 --> 00:03:02.430
I cannot control properly what I do.

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:04.640
On other hand, if I get too strong,

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:06.478
I can start losing flexibility.

00:03:06.478 --> 00:03:08.035
Narrator: It's now about
three hours before the show,

00:03:08.035 --> 00:03:10.430
and Aleksei begins his makeup routine.

00:03:10.430 --> 00:03:12.962
These 45 minutes help
him get into character.

00:03:12.962 --> 00:03:16.651
Aleksei portrays a mythical
creature called an alebrijes.

00:03:16.651 --> 00:03:19.058
Aleksei: It's a Mexican creature that

00:03:19.058 --> 00:03:21.870
combines in itself many different animals

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:25.322
such as swan, panther, scorpion, snake,

00:03:25.322 --> 00:03:28.930
and all these animals are
all in one as alebrijes.

00:03:28.930 --> 00:03:33.128
And this is me. It's my
interpretation of this creature.

00:03:33.128 --> 00:03:34.860
Narrator: He worked
with a choreographer for

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:37.292
six months to bring the creature to life,

00:03:37.292 --> 00:03:39.620
and as his skills have developed

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:41.573
through the years, so has his act.

00:03:42.753 --> 00:03:45.270
Once makeup's done, Aleksei is ready

00:03:45.270 --> 00:03:47.580
to debut his alebrijes
persona to New York City.

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:49.456
But before he comes on in act two,

00:03:49.456 --> 00:03:51.719
other master acrobats take the stage.

00:03:51.719 --> 00:03:53.710
There was hoop-diving on treadmills,

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:56.800
adagio acrobatics, cyr wheel and trapeze,

00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:59.083
hand balancing, masts and poles,

00:03:59.083 --> 00:04:01.200
aerial straps, and juggling.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:04.870
Then finally, a dark form
on a platform is rolled out

00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:08.311
onto a candlelit stage.
The crowd goes dead quiet.

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:15.743
Slowly, Aleksei unravels.

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:20.843
And people shriek.

00:04:22.469 --> 00:04:24.140
Aleksei: Many different
reactions are received.

00:04:24.140 --> 00:04:26.070
Sometimes they are just mesmerized,

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:27.960
and I can see complete
silence in the audience.

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:31.607
I can hear almost nothing
when I perform besides music.

00:04:31.607 --> 00:04:36.170
It's very impressive. You're
just performing in silence.

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:38.450
It's amazing, and the other reaction,

00:04:38.450 --> 00:04:41.224
when they go crazy and
they scream, and sometimes,

00:04:41.224 --> 00:04:44.001
people scream so hard that I cannot hear

00:04:44.001 --> 00:04:48.660
accents in the music. My goal
is to mesmerize, impress,

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:51.295
and to make them go crazy.

00:04:51.295 --> 00:04:53.660
Narrator: He twists and
flips, and you're unsure

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:55.113
which body part is which.

00:04:57.670 --> 00:05:00.113
He fluidly contorts
into shape after shape.

00:05:07.630 --> 00:05:10.963
The best contortionist in the
world strikes his last pose.

00:05:12.699 --> 00:05:15.383
Head between his legs, chest on the floor.

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:18.064
And the audience erupts.

00:05:20.908 --> 00:05:22.520
Aleksei: I really love
it because I realize

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:24.950
how much I can express
myself with my body,

00:05:24.950 --> 00:05:27.828
and I don't need anything
else. Just body, and that's it.

